      "content": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "text": "To divide **391** by **23**, you can use long division:\n\n### Step-by-Step Long Division:\n\n1.  **Divide 39 by 23:**\n    *   23 goes into 39 **1** time (since 23 × 2 = 46, which is too high).\n    *   Write **1** above the 9.\n    *   $39 - 23 = 16$.\n\n2.  **Bring down the 1:**\n    *   Combine the 16 with the 1 to get **161**.\n\n3.  **Divide 161 by 23:**\n    *   From our previous multiplication work, we know that $23 \\times 7 = 161$.\n    *   So, 23 goes into 161 exactly **7** times.\n    *   Write **7** above the 1.\n    *   $161 - 161 = 0$.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n391 ÷ 23 = **17**\n\n***\n\n**Logic Check:**\nSince you just calculated that $23 \\times 17 = 391$, dividing 391 by 23 must equal **17**, as division is the inverse of multiplication.",
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        ],
        "role": "model"
